-- @description Video Preview extension
-- @author Saxmand
-- @version 1.2.1
-- @about
--   # Video Preview extension
--
--   Reads video frames and fingerprints video and audio for the "Video Cut Detection
--   Editor" script package (same repository) - install both, and restart REAPER
--   afterwards.
--
--   What it adds to that script:
--
--   - Cut detection without FFmpeg. It reads a file once into a fingerprint store next
--     to the video, after which detecting again at a different sensitivity is instant
--     rather than another full pass over the file. It also distinguishes a cut from
--     fast motion, which a plain frame-difference threshold cannot.
--   - Video preview frames and cut thumbnails, decoded through AVFoundation.
--   - The Compare Videos tab, which needs this extension: it fingerprints two cuts of
--     the same film, works out which stretches moved where, and conforms a session from
--     one to the other.
--
--   The script works without it by falling back to FFmpeg for cut detection and
--   thumbnails, but the Compare Videos tab is unavailable and cut detection has to
--   re-read the whole file on every run.
--
--   macOS decodes in-process through AVFoundation, which needs nothing installed and
--   fingerprints a file using about a tenth of the CPU a full decode would.
--
--   Windows decodes through Media Foundation, which is part of Windows, so nothing has
--   to be installed there either. What Media Foundation cannot read is ProRes and
--   DNxHD, which have no Windows decoder - for those the extension falls back to the
--   ffmpeg binary if one is available, and the script hands over its path.
--
--   The fingerprints, the cut detector and the matcher are the same code on both
--   platforms, so the results are identical and a store built on one machine can be
--   read on the other.
--
--   macOS: universal binary, Apple Silicon and Intel. Needs macOS 11 on Apple Silicon,
--   10.15 on Intel.
--
--   Windows: 64-bit, and Windows 10 or newer. It links the Universal CRT, which is part
--   of Windows from 10 onwards; on 7 or 8.1 that has to be installed separately through
--   Windows Update.
--
--   Source: Video/extension in this repository.
-- @provides
--   [darwin] reaper_video_preview.dylib
--   [win64] reaper_video_preview-x64.dll
-- @changelog
--   + Fixed: cut detection on Windows found fewer cuts than macOS and put most of them
--     in the wrong place. Every Windows store was labelled 25 fps whatever the file
--     was, because the frame rate was read back off the output format rather than the
--     file's, and cut positions were worked out by dividing a frame number by it. So on
--     anything that was not 25 fps every cut moved, further the later it sat, and the
--     ones pushed past the end of the analysed stretch were dropped.
--   + Cut positions now come from the timestamp each frame carries instead of being
--     divided out of a frame rate, which is also correct for variable frame rate files
--     on either platform. The store's frame rate is measured from those timestamps
--     rather than taken on trust from the decoder.
--   + Fixed: a padded or bottom-up frame buffer on Windows was read as though its rows
--     were packed top-down, which fingerprinted rows of the wrong pixels and, for a
--     bottom-up buffer, read past the end of the buffer.
--   + VP_StoreInfo reports a store's frame count, declared and measured frame rate,
--     timestamp spacing and first hashes, for comparing one machine against another.
